# libraft89

A deterministic Raft consensus core in strict ISO C89. libraft89 owns the
Raft algorithm — leader election, log replication, commit calculation, and
ordered application — and nothing around it.

```text
            application
        +-----------------+
        | storage/network |
        | timers/FSM      |
        +--------+--------+
                 | events / actions
        +--------v--------+
        |    libraft89    |
        | deterministic   |
        | Raft protocol   |
        +-----------------+
```

There are no sockets, threads, files, serialization, event loops, or database
code inside the library. The host supplies messages, commands, logical time,
randomness, and storage reads; every externally visible effect leaves through
an acknowledged action.

## Build and test

- `just build` — build `build/libraft89.a`.
- `just smoke` — one end-to-end lifecycle path.
- `just unit` — unit programs, one per concern.
- `just crash` — crash-point semantics for each durable effect.
- `just sim` — deterministic cluster simulation and seeded random traces.
- `just failalloc` — allocation-failure injection over create, propose, and
  receive (`--wrap`).
- `just test` — smoke, unit, crash, sim, and allocation-failure suites.
- `just exhaustive` — bounded model checker: seeded depth-first exploration
  with the global invariants after every transition. Widen it with
  `MODELFLAGS="-DMODEL_MAX_DEPTH=40ul" just exhaustive`; a state-cap run
  reports `INCONCLUSIVE`.
- `just random` — longer seeded random sweep (100 seeds × 1000 events).
- `just valgrind` — every fast-suite binary under valgrind.
- `just example` — build and run `examples/host_loop.c`.
- `just exhaustive-sanitize` — the model checker under ASan and UBSan.
- `just sanitize` — the fast suite under ASan and UBSan.
- `just check` — the full green profile gate (C89 ∩ C23, GCC and Clang,
  green semantic checks, canonical Allman format).

## Conventions

- Public API namespaced `raft89_*`, declared in `include/raft89.h`.
- The host owns persistent storage; the library reads it through callbacks
  and mutates it through acknowledged actions.
- Exactly one action may be outstanding per node.
- Test-driven: scenario -> acceptance -> failing test -> minimal code ->
  refactor.

See `spec/raft89-spec.md` for the normative contract and `.agent/` for the
concept, design, scenarios, and acceptance criteria.
